    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a little fish character. Draw this exact little fish character as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the round striped yellow-and-blue body, facing right as in image 1, without its tail and without any fin, with a completely blank face — no eye, no mouth — keep the rosy cheek.\n2. the tail: the big yellow fan tail with its orange lines, with a rounded base.\n3. the top fin: the yellow fin on its back with its orange lines, with a rounded base.\n4. the belly fin: one small yellow fin from under its belly, with a rounded base.\n5. the side fin: the small yellow fin that lies on its side in image 1, drawn whole, with a rounded base.\n6. the side fin spread out wide, fanned open, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a little fish character; image 2 shows the same fish cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the fish's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the fish in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the fish's eye as it is in image 1: a big dark round eye with a white sparkle and a white rim.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: the pupil looking down, its upper lid drooping and tilted, a thin shine of a welling tear along the bottom rim.\n6. the same eye crying: gently squeezed shut, a soft downward-curving line (a sad closed eye, not a smile), a few small lashes, and one small light-blue teardrop just below it.\n7. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile.\n8. the mouth laughing: open wide, a little pink inside.\n9. the mouth puckered into a small round \"o\", blowing.\n10. the mouth sad: a small downturned frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
